=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) as a design paradigm centered on objects. These objects serve as models for real-world or abstract entities and are defined by two main components: data (attributes/properties) and behavior (methods/functions).

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
