This segment compares classes and structs, highlighting their differences in access modifiers, encapsulation, and use cases. While Java exclusively uses classes, C++ supports both. The main distinctions are that structs default to public access and offer less encapsulation support, making them suitable for lightweight objects. In contrast, classes default to private access and provide full encapsulation support for all types of object-oriented programming needs.

