This table of contents outlines the foundational topics for learning UML. It begins with an introduction to object-oriented principles such as encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism. It then provides a historical overview of UML and categorizes its diagrams into structure and behavior types. Finally, it focuses on Use Case Diagrams, covering the identification of actors and use cases, as well as the relationships between them, providing a roadmap for modeling system requirements.

