=== SUMMARY ===
This Table of Contents segment outlines core UML modeling concepts across three main chapters. Chapter 3 concludes Use Case Diagrams by discussing pitfalls and practical examples. Chapter 4 provides an in-depth exploration of Class Diagrams, covering notation, attributes, associations, inheritance, and the distinction between abstract classes and interfaces. Chapter 5 focuses on State Machine Diagrams, detailing state types, transitions, events, and advanced concepts like composite and history states. Together, these sections establish the framework for structural and behavioral system modeling and subsequent code generation.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
