=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the standard notation for UML diagram frames and the use of notes. A diagram frame consists of a rectangle with a pentagon in the top-left corner indicating the diagram type (e.g., ''cd'' for class diagrams, ''sd'' for sequence diagrams) and its name. The text also introduces ''notes'' as a universal concept for adding precise details or constraints to model elements. Notes can be written in natural language or Object Constraint Language (OCL) to clarify rules not easily captured by graphical notation.

