=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces four essential UML behavior diagrams: Activity, Sequence, Communication, and Timing. The Activity Diagram models business and software processes using control and data flows. The Sequence Diagram focuses on the chronological order of messages between objects, while the Communication Diagram prioritizes the relationships between interaction partners over timing. Finally, the Timing Diagram illustrates state changes triggered by time events or message exchanges. These diagrams collectively allow developers to define how a system''s objects interact and how processes are executed in detail.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
