=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains extension points and generalization in use case diagrams. Extension points allow specific behaviors to be inserted into a base use case. Generalization enables a child use case to inherit behavior and relationships from a parent, allowing it to extend or overwrite functionality. The text also defines abstract use cases, which cannot be executed directly and only serve as templates for specific child use cases. This structure helps organize common properties and ensures proper actor-use case associations.

