=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the structure and notation of classes in UML diagrams. Classes use attributes to store instance-specific data and operations to define object behavior. A key principle discussed is abstraction, which involves including only system-relevant information to manage complexity. In UML notation, a class is depicted as a rectangle with three compartments: the class name (singular noun, bold, capitalized), the attributes, and the operations. The level of detail shown in these compartments can vary depending on the specific requirements of the software development phase.

