=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the structure and notation of classes within UML class diagrams. Classes use compartments for names, attributes, and operations, with the level of detail increasing as software development progresses—from abstract analysis to implementation-ready code generation. It highlights naming conventions, where class names typically start with uppercase letters while attributes and operations start with lowercase. Additionally, it introduces the syntax for attribute specification, which includes mandatory names and optional elements like types (primitive, composite, or user-defined), visibility, and multiplicities.

