=== SUMMARY ===
This chapter introduces Design Patterns as a way to leverage the collective wisdom of developers to solve common software design challenges. Moving beyond simple code reuse, patterns offer "experience reuse" by providing proven templates for flexible and maintainable code. Using the SimUDuck application as a case study, it explores core OO principles like encapsulating what varies and favoring composition over inheritance ("HAS-A" over "IS-A"). The goal is to build designs that can easily adapt to change through a shared vocabulary of patterns.

