=== SUMMARY ===
This segment details how to define advanced attribute characteristics in UML class diagrams. It covers default values, which ensure attributes are never empty, and properties like {readOnly} that prevent changes after initialization. It introduces derived attributes, marked with a forward slash (/), whose values are calculated from other data. Finally, it explains multiplicities, which specify the number of values an attribute can hold (similar to arrays), represented as intervals in square brackets.

