This segment explains UML multiplicity and operation specifications. Multiplicity, denoted as [min..max], defines how many values an attribute can hold, with ''*'' indicating no upper limit and ''1'' being the default. Attributes with multiple values can be further refined as sets, multi-sets, ordered sets, or lists using properties like {unique} and {ordered}. Additionally, operations are defined by their name, parameters, and return types, functioning similarly to method declarations in programming to represent an object''s behavior.

