=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the specification of operations in UML class diagrams. It details how operations are defined by their signatures, including names, parameters, and return types, while noting that implementation details are reserved for behavior diagrams. The text covers parameter syntax—where only the name is mandatory—and the use of parameter directions: ''in'' (default), ''out'', and ''inout''. Notably, ''out'' parameters allow operations to return multiple values, as demonstrated by the ''getName'' example. Class diagrams essentially model the interfaces of object behavior.

