=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces the State Machine Diagram, a UML tool used to model the lifecycle of a system or object through its finite states. It explains how events trigger state transitions and describes the behavior exhibited in each state. Based on finite automata and David Harel''s work, the text distinguishes between behavior and protocol state machines. It emphasizes that the complexity of these diagrams varies according to the development phase, from high-level documentation to detailed code-oriented representations.

