=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the use of pseudostates in state machine diagrams, focusing on decision, parallelization, and synchronization nodes. Decision nodes allow for alternative transitions based on guard evaluations, noting that the sequence of activities and guard checks affects semantic behavior. Parallelization nodes split a flow into concurrent transitions, while synchronization nodes merge multiple concurrent flows. Both are represented as black bars but serve different structural purposes. The text highlights that these control structures do not consume time and have specific rules regarding guards and events.

