=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains specialized UML events: Change Events, Any Receive Events, and Completion Events. It contrasts Change Events, which trigger transitions immediately when a condition becomes true, with guards, which are only checked when a specific event occurs. The ''any receive event'' (labeled ''all'') acts as a default ''else'' transition for unexpected events. Finally, a Completion Event occurs once all activities and nested states within a state are finished, automatically triggering any outgoing transition that lacks a specific event label.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. What is the primary difference between a change event and a guard in terms of when they are evaluated?
2. How does an ''any receive event'' function within a state machine, and what keyword is used to represent it?
