=== SUMMARY ===
This table summarizes the essential notation elements of UML state machine diagrams. It defines structural components like states (with entry, do, and exit activities) and transitions between them. It also covers lifecycle nodes (initial, final, and terminate), flow control nodes (decision, parallelization, and synchronization), and history states. These elements provide a standardized visual language to model the complete lifecycle and behavioral logic of a system or object, including complex logic like branching and concurrent execution.

