=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains interaction partners in UML sequence diagrams, represented by lifelines. Lifelines use the format ''roleName:Class'' to identify partners at both instance and class levels. The text highlights the flexibility of the ''role'' concept, which allows a single object to assume different behaviors over time without needing dynamic class changes. It also introduces specialized lifelines: multivalued roles that use selectors (like indices) to identify specific objects, and active objects which represent independent threads of control or processes.

