=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the visual representation and structural logic of UML sequence diagrams. Key concepts include active objects, which represent independent processes or threads and are marked by a double boundary on the lifeline head. The diagram uses a two-dimensional layout where the horizontal axis lists interaction partners and the vertical axis represents chronological time. Events like sending and receiving messages are modeled as event specifications, while bars on the lifeline denote execution specifications, showing when an object is actively performing a behavior.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. How does a lifeline representing an active object differ visually from a standard lifeline?
2. What is the specific purpose of using ''self'' in the head of a lifeline?
