=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains how sequence diagrams model message exchanges and chronological ordering. The vertical axis represents time, determining event sequences on individual lifelines, while message exchanges establish order across different lifelines. Valid sequences are called traces; multiple traces may exist if messages lack common interaction partners. Additionally, the text introduces execution specifications—visualized as bars—to indicate behavior duration. It distinguishes between direct execution (performed by the object) and indirect execution (delegated to others), often resulting in overlapping bars during self-calls.

