=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the visualization of execution specifications and messages in UML sequence diagrams. Execution specifications, shown as bars on lifelines, indicate when an object is performing a behavior. Messages are depicted as arrows: synchronous messages use filled arrowheads and require the sender to wait for a response, while asynchronous messages use open arrowheads and allow the sender to proceed immediately. Response messages are represented by dashed lines. Although execution specifications are optional, they clarify the timing and delegation of tasks between interaction partners.

