=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains UML combined fragments used to control execution flow and message ordering in sequence diagrams. It covers the ''loop'' and ''break'' fragments for handling repetitions and exceptions. It also defines the ''seq'' (weak sequencing) fragment, which maintains event order within operands and on the same lifelines while allowing flexibility for events on different lifelines. Additionally, it describes how ''seq'' fragments can be combined with ''break'' fragments to manage execution when specific conditions trigger an exit from a sequence of messages.

