=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the functionality of ''seq'' and ''strict'' fragments in UML sequence diagrams. The ''seq'' fragment represents weak sequencing, where events on different lifelines can interleave unless a direct message link exists. Using ''seq'' explicitly allows a ''break'' fragment to exit a specific scope rather than the entire diagram. Conversely, the ''strict'' fragment enforces a rigid chronological order based solely on the vertical position of messages, regardless of whether the lifelines involved interact directly.

