registration
possible
enrolled
{examDate>now}

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains time constraints and state invariants in UML sequence diagrams. Time constraints define when events occur using expressions like absolute time, relative time, or intervals. State invariants are conditions assigned to lifelines that must be true before the next event. If an invariant is false, the system''s model or implementation is flawed. Invariants can be shown using curly brackets, notes, or rounded rectangles. They ensure prerequisites, such as being enrolled or meeting deadlines, are satisfied before an interaction proceeds.

