=== SUMMARY ===
This section explains how to create sequence diagrams by focusing on two main scenarios: establishing the link between class diagrams and sequence diagrams, and describing design patterns. It emphasizes that UML diagrams are interdependent views of the same system content. Using a university administration example, it illustrates how structural elements defined in a class diagram—such as classes for students, courses, and registrations—form the essential foundation for the dynamic interactions modeled in sequence diagrams.

