node then has multiple incoming edges and multiple outgoing edges.
For decision and merge nodes, only one of the possible paths is ac-
tive. As already mentioned, you can use multiple initial nodes to model
concurrency at the beginning of an activity. If an execution path splits
into multiple simultaneously active execution paths later on, you can re-
alize this using a parallelization node. A parallelization node is depicted
