when both the lecture and the assignment have been completed (see next
paragraph).
You can merge concurrent subpaths using a synchronization node.
Synchronization node
...
This node is the counterpart to the parallelization node. It is depicted as
a black bar with multiple incoming edges but only one outgoing edge.
As soon as tokens are present at all incoming edges, that is, as soon
as all preceding actions have been executed, all incoming tokens are
merged into one token that is passed on at the outgoing edge.

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment details essential control nodes in UML activity diagrams: merge, parallelization, and synchronization nodes. A merge node (diamond) reunites alternative paths and can create loops when paired with decision nodes. Concurrency is managed via parallelization nodes (black bars), which split a flow into multiple active paths, and synchronization nodes, which join concurrent paths back into one. Crucially, a synchronization node only releases a token once all incoming paths have completed their execution and provided tokens.

