An action can only be executed if tokens are present at all of its
incoming edges. If an action has multiple outgoing edges, a token is
offered to all target nodes of these edges, thereby causing a split into
multiple independent execution paths. Special nodes are also available
as an alternative for modeling this concurrency. We will look at these in
more detail later on.
When an action is executed, usually one token of each of its incom-
ing edges is consumed. Alternatively, a weight may be placed on an
Weight of an edge
A
B
