=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains Object Flows in UML Activity Diagrams, focusing on how data tokens are handled. It describes object nodes and pin notation for action inputs and outputs. Two specialized nodes are introduced: the Central Buffer and the Data Store. A Central Buffer acts as transient storage where data is removed once consumed. Conversely, a Data Store provides permanent storage, copying tokens so they remain available for multiple uses, effectively modeling database-like functionality with support for content queries.

