=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces partitions in UML activity diagrams, also known as swimlanes. Partitions group actions and edges based on common properties, such as organizational roles or responsibilities, to improve clarity. Crucially, partitions provide a logical view and do not influence the token flow or execution semantics of the activity. They can be represented as open rectangles, can be nested into subpartitions, and can reach various levels of detail, from organizational units down to individual classes.

