7.6 Exception Handling
If an error occurs during the execution of an action, the execution is ter-
minated. In this situation, there is no guarantee that the action will de-
liver the expected output. If an action has an exception handler for a spe-
Exception handler
Exception-
Handler
Action
e
ciﬁc error situation, this exception handler is activated when an excep-
tion occurs. Using an exception handler, you can deﬁne how the system
is to react in a speciﬁc error situation e. This allows you to minimize the
effects of this error. You specify an exception handler for a speciﬁc type
of error—that is, you can use different exception handlers for different
errors. If an error situation occurs, all tokens in the action concerned
are deleted immediately. If there is a matching exception handler, this
replaces the content of the action concerned and instead, the content of
the exception handler is executed. The sequence then continues as the
regular path of the activity as if the defective action had ended normally.
As an exception handler is an activity node, it is depicted as a rectangle
with rounded corners. The action safeguarded by the exception handler
points to the exception handler with a lightning bolt arrow. The tip of
the arrow is labeled with the type of the error. Figure 7.25 shows two
examples for handling exceptions. If a paper jam occurs during printing,
printing can continue once the paper jam has been removed. If there is
no paper in the printer, paper must be inserted for printing to continue
until sufﬁcient copies of the exam instructions have been printed.

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment details textual notation for partitions and the mechanics of exception handling in activity diagrams. Textual notation uses parentheses and double colons to represent multi-dimensional and hierarchical partitions. Exception handling provides a way to manage errors by replacing a failed action''s content with a handler''s execution. When an exception occurs, tokens are deleted, and the handler is activated via a lightning bolt arrow labeled with the error type. Once the handler finishes, the activity resumes its regular path, minimizing the impact of the error.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. How is a hierarchical relationship between a partition and a subpartition represented using textual notation?
2. What happens to the control tokens of an action when a matching exception handler is triggered?
3. Which visual symbol is used to connect a safeguarded action to its corresponding exception handler?
4. After an exception handler completes its execution, how does the flow of the activity diagram proceed?','7fc4954d-6736-4f6c-8047-4cce182ae649'::uuid,NULL,NULL,169,786,'2026-05-08 16:23:24.149765+07');
