2. How does the UML infrastructure function in relation to the metamodel?
3. Why might representing a generalization as a separate class be beneficial in a complex metamodel?
4. In what scenarios does the text suggest that standard UML might be too general for practical use?','73a99556-1722-4edc-937d-cadf12e8abc1'::uuid,NULL,NULL,197,907,'2026-05-08 16:23:24.15274+07');
