=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces the Observer Pattern, a fundamental design pattern used to create one-to-many relationships between objects. By using a ''Subject'' and multiple ''Observers'' (similar to publishers and subscribers), the pattern ensures that when one object changes state, all its dependents are notified and updated automatically. The text emphasizes the power of loose coupling to create flexible and maintainable systems. It also connects the pattern to core OO principles, specifically the goal of striving for loosely coupled designs between interacting objects.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
