=== SUMMARY ===
This chapter introduces the Factory Patterns as a means to achieve loosely coupled designs by encapsulating object instantiation. It explains how using the ''new'' operator publicly can create problematic dependencies. The content covers the Simple Factory, Factory Method Pattern, and Abstract Factory Pattern, using a pizza store example to illustrate these concepts. Additionally, it explores the Dependency Inversion Principle, which encourages depending on abstractions rather than concrete classes, and provides a comparative analysis of different factory implementations.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
