=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces the Command Pattern, which focuses on encapsulating method invocation. By turning requests into objects, the pattern decouples the object that invokes the computation from the one that executes it. This abstraction allows for advanced features such as implementing undo/redo functionality, logging requests, and queuing tasks. Using a diner analogy (Customer, Order, Waitress, Cook), the text explains how these roles translate into software components like the Client, Command, Invoker, and Receiver to create flexible, maintainable systems like home automation controllers.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. What does it mean to ''encapsulate method invocation'' according to the text?
