=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces the Template Method Pattern, which encapsulates the skeleton of an algorithm in a base class. By generalizing common steps (like boiling water) into a superclass and delegating specific steps (like brewing coffee versus steeping tea) to subclasses, the pattern allows for code reuse and structured flexibility. It also explores ''hooks'' for optional algorithmic steps and the ''Hollywood Principle,'' which maintains a clean dependency structure by letting high-level components control when low-level components are called.

