=== SUMMARY ===
This chapter explores the Proxy Pattern, a structural design pattern used to control and manage access to objects. By acting as a surrogate or placeholder, a proxy can handle remote communication, defer the creation of expensive objects (Virtual Proxy), or manage access permissions (Protection Proxy). The text covers technical implementations including Remote Method Invocation (RMI), the use of Java''s InvocationHandler for dynamic proxies, and practical examples like a remote GumballMachine monitor and an album cover viewer.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
