=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces Compound Patterns, where multiple design patterns work together to solve complex object-oriented design problems. It highlights Model-View-Controller (MVC) as the quintessential example, often called the ''King of Compound Patterns.'' The text explores how MVC integrates patterns like Strategy, Observer, and Composite to manage state, behavior, and user interface updates. By using a ''BeatModel'' example, it demonstrates the flow of information between the controller, model, and view, showing how compound patterns create flexible and maintainable software architectures.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. What are ''compound patterns'' and how do they differ from individual design patterns?
