=== SUMMARY ===
This appendix introduces the remaining official Gang of Four (GoF) design patterns that, while less commonly used than those previously discussed, are still powerful tools for specific scenarios. It provides a high-level overview of patterns like Bridge, Builder, Chain of Responsibility, Flyweight, Interpreter, Mediator, Memento, Prototype, and Visitor. Using the Visitor pattern as an example, it demonstrates how these patterns can add functionality to existing structures, such as a Composite, without needing to modify the original classes, thereby maintaining clean object-oriented designs.

