=== SUMMARY ===
This segment demonstrates how to make object behaviors dynamic by adding setter methods to the Duck class. By implementing setFlyBehavior and setQuackBehavior, the program can change a duck''s behavior at runtime rather than being restricted to the initial assignment in the constructor. The example uses a ModelDuck and a new FlyRocketPowered behavior to show how a duck that starts as non-flying can be dynamically upgraded to fly with a rocket, highlighting the flexibility of the Strategy Pattern.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. What is the primary advantage of using setter methods for behaviors instead of only initializing them in the constructor?
2. In the provided code, what are the initial flying and quacking behaviors assigned to the ModelDuck?
3. How does the FlyRocketPowered class interact with the existing Duck design to provide new functionality?
4. Which specific class must be modified to ensure all duck subclasses inherit the ability to change their behaviors dynamically?','c9b733bd-f203-4d04-956d-bf5bb33fd3e9'::uuid,NULL,NULL,58,586,'2026-05-08 16:43:33.918513+07');
