=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces a requirement change in the SimUDuck application: the need for ducks to fly. To implement this, Joe decides to add a ''fly()'' method to the Duck superclass. By doing so, he leverages inheritance so that all existing and future duck subclasses, like MallardDuck and RedheadDuck, automatically gain flying behavior. This illustrates a common initial approach in object-oriented design where inheritance is used for code reuse across multiple subclasses.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. Why did Joe''s company decide to add flying functionality to the SimUDuck application?
2. What specific object-oriented technique did Joe use to ensure all ducks could fly?
3. In Joe''s design, which class contains the implementation of the ''fly()'' method?
4. According to the text, what is the expected result for subclasses like MallardDuck when ''fly()'' is added to the superclass?','861dd46c-9739-4571-ac2e-edd5f3e2f8ae'::uuid,NULL,NULL,41,419,'2026-05-08 16:43:33.916843+07');
