=== SUMMARY ===
This segment provides a comprehensive class diagram for the redesigned SimUDuck application. It introduces the concept of viewing behaviors as a "family of algorithms" that are encapsulated and interchangeable. By using interfaces for flying and quacking behaviors, the system achieves greater flexibility. The text emphasizes identifying key object-oriented relationships—IS-A (inheritance), HAS-A (composition), and IMPLEMENTS (interface realization)—to understand how the client (Duck) utilizes these encapsulated algorithms to perform actions without being tied to specific implementations.

