=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces the OO Design Toolbox, categorizing essential knowledge into OO Basics, Principles, and Patterns. It emphasizes that basic concepts like inheritance are insufficient for high-quality design. Instead, good design requires principles like encapsulating variation and favoring composition. Design patterns, such as the Strategy pattern, offer time-tested solutions to recurring problems. They are discovered through experience rather than invented, providing a shared language for developers to create maintainable, flexible systems that handle change effectively by decoupling varying parts from the rest of the application.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. According to the text, why is knowing OO basics like inheritance and polymorphism not enough to be a good designer?
