cutting with a knife }
Design Puzzle Solution
Note that ANY object could
implement the WeaponBehavior
interface—say, a paper clip, a tube of
toastepaste, or a mutated sea bass.
Abstract
A Character HAS-A
WeaponBehavior.

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment illustrates a solution to a design puzzle using the Strategy Pattern. It defines an abstract Character class that employs composition through a ''HAS-A'' relationship with a WeaponBehavior interface. Specific characters (King, Queen, etc.) inherit from Character, while various weapon actions implement the WeaponBehavior interface. This design allows characters to dynamically swap weapons at runtime using the setWeapon() method, effectively encapsulating weapon-specific algorithms and separating them from the character types that use them.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. What is the structural relationship (e.g., HAS-A or IS-A) between the Character class and the WeaponBehavior interface?
