3. Why are specific weapon behaviors like AxeBehavior and SwordBehavior implemented as classes that satisfy an interface rather than being hardcoded into the Character class?
4. What is the purpose of making the Character class abstract instead of concrete in this specific design solution?','34fec1bc-a0c1-4479-849b-06398038219e'::uuid,NULL,NULL,72,582,'2026-05-08 16:43:33.919973+07');
