=== SUMMARY ===
This segment illustrates a flawed initial implementation of the WeatherData class. By hard-coding updates to specific display objects within the measurementsChanged method, the design becomes rigid. Key issues identified include coding to concrete implementations rather than interfaces, the inability to add or remove displays at runtime, and failing to encapsulate the changing parts of the code. This example serves as a critique to demonstrate why a more flexible approach, like the Observer Pattern, is necessary for maintaining and extending software.

