This segment challenges readers to apply the Observer Pattern by sketching a class diagram for a Weather Station system. It emphasizes defining the relationships between the WeatherData class and various display elements. The goal is to create a design where components are structured logically and new developers can easily add custom display elements without disrupting the existing system. This exercise reinforces the practical application of loose coupling and interface-based design before moving into the implementation phase.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. What are the two main types of components you need to identify when sketching the Weather Station design?
2. How should the WeatherData class and the display elements relate to each other according to the Observer Pattern?
3. In your diagram, how would you ensure that the system is extensible for other developers to add their own displays?
