Code to set up the frame goes here.
use action listener observers

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment demonstrates a practical application of the Observer Pattern using Java''s Swing library. It shows how a JButton acts as a Subject by allowing multiple ActionListener objects (Observers) to register interest in its state changes. When the button is clicked, it notifies all registered listeners by calling their actionPerformed() method. The example uses inner classes (AngelListener and DevilListener) to implement specific response behaviors, illustrating how the pattern decouples the UI component from the specific actions triggered by user interaction.

