until I learned the power of
extension at runtime, rather than
at compile time. Now look at me!

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces the Decorator Pattern as a powerful alternative to inheritance. It explains how to use object composition to extend the functionality of objects at runtime rather than at compile time. By mastering this pattern, developers can add new responsibilities to existing objects without modifying the original code of the underlying classes, effectively preventing the issues associated with subclassing everything and providing more flexibility in class design.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. What common design problem is the Decorator Pattern intended to address?
2. How does the Decorator Pattern differ from subclassing in terms of when extension occurs?
3. What mechanism does the Decorator Pattern use to add new responsibilities to objects?
4. What is the primary benefit of being able to decorate objects without changing their underlying source code?','2b954424-2826-4b79-b67d-5973ffa0506f'::uuid,NULL,NULL,117,383,'2026-05-08 16:43:33.924103+07');
