=== SUMMARY ===
This segment illustrates how the Java I/O library utilizes the Decorator Pattern to manage its extensive class library. It identifies FileInputStream as a concrete component that provides basic byte-reading capabilities. Classes like BufferedInputStream and ZipInputStream act as concrete decorators, adding specialized behaviors such as performance buffering and zip-file processing. Understanding this pattern helps developers navigate the complex java.io package by recognizing that complex functionality is achieved by wrapping base components with multiple layers of decorators.

