=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains how the Java I/O library utilizes the Decorator Pattern. It identifies InputStream as the abstract component and FilterInputStream as the abstract decorator, with classes like BufferedInputStream acting as concrete decorators. It notes that while the pattern allows for flexible behavior wrapping, a significant downside is the creation of many small classes that can be overwhelming to developers. This design pattern is consistently applied across input/output streams and character-based Reader/Writer classes, enabling developers to compose complex functionalities through object wrapping.

