=== SUMMARY ===
This segment reviews essential Object-Oriented design tools, emphasizing the Open-Closed Principle: classes should be open for extension but closed for modification. It introduces the Decorator Pattern as a dynamic alternative to subclassing for extending functionality. Decorators wrap components to add behavior at runtime using composition and delegation. While they offer flexibility and maintain type transparency, the pattern can lead to designs with many small objects, potentially increasing complexity if overused or if clients depend on specific concrete types.

