why don’t you take a crack at building the Chicago-style and
California-style pizza stores on the next page?
Here’s where we create our
concrete classes. For each type of
Pizza we create the NY style.
* Note that the orderPizza() method in the
superclass has no clue which Pizza we are creating;
it just knows it can prepare, bake, cut, and box it!
createPizza() returns a Pizza, and
the subclass is fully responsible for
which concrete Pizza it instantiates.

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains how to apply the Factory Method pattern by creating the NYPizzaStore subclass. By extending the abstract PizzaStore class, the regional store inherits standard functionality like orderPizza() but must implement the abstract createPizza() method. This delegation allows subclasses to decide which concrete pizza types (e.g., NYStyleCheesePizza) to instantiate. This design decouples the high-level ordering logic from specific product creation, ensuring that the superclass can process pizzas without knowing their specific regional styles or ingredients.

