This segment presents a ''DependentPizzaStore'' class that avoids using a factory. It demonstrates tight coupling by showing how the store directly instantiates eight concrete pizza classes across two different regional styles (NY and Chicago). This example serves as a cautionary lesson in object-oriented design, highlighting how direct instantiation makes code rigid, hard to maintain, and heavily dependent on specific implementations rather than abstractions. Adding new products would further increase these dependencies and complexity within the high-level class.

