=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains how to apply the Dependency Inversion Principle (DIP) to decouple high-level and low-level components. Initially, the PizzaStore (high-level) was dependent on many concrete pizza types (low-level). By implementing the Factory Method Pattern, both the PizzaStore and the concrete pizza classes are made to depend on the abstract Pizza class. This reduction in direct dependencies makes the system more flexible and robust, illustrating how high-level modules and low-level modules should both rely on abstractions rather than concrete implementations.

