=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces the concept of product families within the Factory Pattern. It explains that while all pizzas consist of similar components like dough, sauce, and cheese, different regions (New York, Chicago, California) require specific implementations of these ingredients. The challenge is to manage these related groups of products as the business expands to new locations. By organizing ingredients into "families," the system can ensure that each regional franchise uses the correct, consistent set of components intended for its specific style.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
