146	 	 Chapter 4
ingredient factories
public interface PizzaIngredientFactory {
public Dough createDough();
public Sauce createSauce();
public Cheese createCheese();
public Veggies[] createVeggies();
public Pepperoni createPepperoni();
public Clams createClam();
}
Building the ingredient factories
Now we’re going to build a factory to create our ingredients; the
factory will be responsible for creating each ingredient in the
ingredient family. In other words, the factory will need to create
dough, sauce, cheese, and so on... You’ll see how we are going to
handle the regional differences shortly.
Let’s start by defining an interface for the factory that is going to
create all our ingredients:
For each ingredient we define a
create method in our interface.
With that interface, here’s what we’re going to do:
Lots of new classes here,
one per ingredient.
1
2
3
Build a factory for each region. To do this, you’ll create a subclass of
PizzaIngredientFactory that implements each create method.
Implement a set of ingredient classes to be used with the factory, like
ReggianoCheese, RedPeppers, and ThickCrustDough. These classes can be
shared among regions where appropriate.
Then we still need to hook all this up by working our new ingredient
factories into our old PizzaStore code.

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces the Abstract Factory pattern for managing ingredient families. It defines the ''PizzaIngredientFactory'' interface, which includes methods for creating various pizza components like dough, sauce, and cheese. The approach involves three steps: creating regional factory subclasses, implementing specific ingredient classes (some of which can be shared), and integrating these factories into the existing PizzaStore code. This structure ensures that each franchise uses consistent ingredients tailored to their specific region while maintaining a flexible, decoupled design.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. What is the specific purpose of the PizzaIngredientFactory interface?
2. How are regional differences in pizza ingredients handled within this factory framework?
3. What are the three steps outlined for implementing the ingredient factory system?
4. Why does the text suggest that some ingredient classes can be shared among different regions?','fc7ec658-bea0-4327-bb85-8dbd0a9aeff8'::uuid,NULL,NULL,184,575,'2026-05-08 16:43:33.930869+07');
