=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the Abstract Factory pattern, which provides an interface for creating families of related products, such as pizza ingredients. By coding to this interface rather than concrete implementations, the system becomes decoupled from specific product variations. This allows developers to swap factories to suit different contexts (like different regions) without changing the client code. Consequently, the same pizza-making logic can produce different results simply by substituting one concrete ingredient factory for another.

