INSERT INTO coaching_chatbot.lecture_knowledge_chunks (lecture_knowledge_chunks_id,lecture_knowledge_id,chunk_index,chunk_content,qdrant_point_id,start_time_seconds,end_time_seconds,page_number,token_count,created_at) VALUES ('a01cb5ab-5559-480e-a454-64c27bf5c2f7'::uuid,'56576a1d-5b81-4e06-824c-2a0e45e5a305'::uuid,224,'=== ORIGINAL CONTENT ===
you are here 4    189
the singleton pattern
public class ChocolateBoiler {
private boolean empty;
private boolean boiled;
private static ChocolateBoiler uniqueInstance;
private ChocolateBoiler() {
empty = true;
boiled = false;
}
public static ChocolateBoiler getInstance() {
if (uniqueInstance == null) {
uniqueInstance = new ChocolateBoiler();
}
return uniqueInstance;
}
public void fill() {
if (isEmpty()) {
empty = false;
boiled = false;
// fill the boiler with a milk/chocolate mixture
}
}
// rest of ChocolateBoiler code...
}
Can you help Choc-O-Holic improve their ChocolateBoiler class
by turning it into a Singleton?

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment demonstrates how to implement the Singleton Pattern using a ChocolateBoiler class example. By using a private constructor, the class prevents external instantiation. It provides a static getInstance() method that ensures only one instance of the boiler is created and shared across the application. This ''lazy instantiation'' approach helps manage shared resources efficiently. The exercise challenges learners to identify how this structure maintains a single point of access and prevents the creation of multiple, conflicting instances of the boiler.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. Why is the constructor of the ChocolateBoiler class declared as private instead of public?
2. What is the purpose of the ''uniqueInstance'' static variable within the class?
3. How does the getInstance() method ensure that a new instance is only created when necessary?
4. Identify a potential problem that could occur with this specific implementation in a multithreaded environment.','0659f183-f646-4773-9528-f4ce2ae622bf'::uuid,NULL,NULL,227,410,'2026-05-08 16:43:33.935308+07');
