=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces the physical interface of the Home Automation Remote Control prototype. It features seven programmable slots, each equipped with dedicated ON and OFF buttons to control various household devices. A key feature is the inclusion of a global undo button, which reverses the last action taken. This hardware layout serves as the practical requirement for the upcoming Command Pattern implementation, emphasizing the need for a flexible system that can map physical button presses to diverse device operations across multiple slots.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
