An invoker — for instance,
one slot of the remote —
can be parameterized with
different requests.
The Command Pattern encapsulates a request as an
object, thereby letting you parameterize other objects
with different requests, queue or log requests, and
support undoable operations.

=== SUMMARY ===
The Command Pattern encapsulates a request as an object by binding a set of actions to a specific receiver. This encapsulation allows invokers to trigger requests via a single execute() method without knowing the underlying details of the receiver or the actions performed. This pattern enables objects to be parameterized with different requests and supports advanced functionalities such as queuing, logging, undoable operations, and the Meta Command Pattern, which allows for the creation of command macros.

