=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the Command Pattern class diagram, detailing the roles of the Client, Invoker, Command interface, ConcreteCommand, and Receiver. The pattern encapsulates a request as an object by binding a receiver to an action within a ConcreteCommand. This structure decouples the object making the request (Invoker) from the object that performs the work (Receiver). By using a common Command interface with execute() and undo() methods, the Invoker can trigger various requests without knowing the specific details of the actions or the receivers involved.

