=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains how the Command Pattern can be extended to support logging and crash recovery by adding store() and load() methods. Instead of saving an entire large data structure (like a spreadsheet) after every change, applications can log individual command objects to disk. In the event of a system failure, these commands are reloaded and re-executed in sequence from the last checkpoint to restore the state. This technique also provides a foundation for implementing transactional behavior in advanced applications.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
