=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces the Object-Oriented Adapter pattern as a solution for integrating incompatible software interfaces. When an existing system needs to use a new vendor library with a different interface, an adapter acts as a middleman. It implements the interface the system expects while translating requests into calls the vendor''s class understands. This approach allows integration without modifying the original system''s code or the vendor''s library, effectively solving interface mismatch problems while maintaining a clean separation of concerns.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. What is the primary function of an adapter when integrating a new vendor class into an existing system?
