Simple implementations: MallardDuck
just prints out what it is doing.
Now it’s time to meet the newest fowl on the block:
Turkeys don’t quack, they gobble.
Turkeys can fly, although they
can only fly short distances.

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces the core components for demonstrating the Adapter Pattern using a ''Duck'' and ''Turkey'' analogy. It defines the Duck interface, which includes quacking and flying, and its implementation, MallardDuck. It then introduces the Turkey interface, which uses different method names like ''gobble'' and has different flight characteristics. This setup establishes the problem of interface incompatibility, where a system expecting a Duck interface needs to work with a Turkey object, laying the groundwork for the creation of an adapter class.

