This segment explains how to apply the Adapter pattern to bridge legacy Java code with modern interfaces by adapting an Enumeration to an Iterator. It identifies that while hasNext() and next() map easily to hasMoreElements() and nextElement(), the remove() method presents a challenge because Enumeration is a read-only interface. The proposed design uses an EnumerationIterator class that implements the Iterator interface (the Target) and uses composition to delegate calls to an Enumeration object (the Adaptee), allowing new code to interact with old collections seamlessly.

