=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the practical need for adapting modern Java Iterators to legacy Enumeration interfaces to support older client code. It proposes a coding exercise using an ArrayList, which natively lacks Enumeration support, to demonstrate this conversion. Furthermore, it introduces a conceptual distinction between simply changing an interface (Adapter pattern) and adding new responsibilities or features to an object, prompting the reader to identify the appropriate design pattern for extending behavior, such as the Decorator pattern.

