This segment introduces Chapter 8, which focuses on the Template Method Pattern. After covering the encapsulation of object creation and interfaces, the text explains that this pattern involves encapsulating pieces of algorithms. This structure allows subclasses to hook into a computation at specific points. Additionally, it teases a new design principle inspired by Hollywood, setting the stage for deeper exploration into algorithmic structure and subclass integration.

