This segment explains how to enable sorting for a custom class in Java by implementing the Comparable interface. It details the implementation of the compareTo() method within a Duck class, which defines the sorting criteria based on weight. This allows the Arrays.sort() template method to compare Duck objects effectively. The method returns -1, 0, or 1 to indicate if the current object is less than, equal to, or greater than the object being compared, providing the essential logic for the sorting algorithm.

