using iterator

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains how to implement the Iterator Pattern by defining a custom Iterator interface and a concrete implementation, DinerMenuIterator. It demonstrates how to encapsulate traversal logic for an array-based collection. The Iterator interface uses hasNext() to check for remaining elements and next() to retrieve them. The DinerMenuIterator handles array boundaries and potential null values, ensuring the client can iterate through menu items consistently without knowing the underlying data structure. This encapsulation promotes loose coupling between the menu implementation and its clients.

