=== SUMMARY ===
This segment provides a matching exercise to help students distinguish between three similar design patterns: State, Strategy, and Template Method. It focuses on their core definitions: the State pattern manages state-based behavior via delegation; the Strategy pattern uses delegation for interchangeable behaviors; and the Template Method relies on subclasses to implement specific steps of an algorithm. This exercise reinforces the conceptual boundaries and specific implementation mechanisms—such as delegation versus inheritance—used by each pattern to manage behavioral variations.

