Walking through the design

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the Remote Proxy pattern through the use of helper objects. It describes how a ''client helper'' acts as a local proxy, pretending to be the actual service to intercept method calls. This helper handles network communication, forwarding requests to a ''service helper'' on the server. The service helper then invokes the method on the real service object. This design allows remote communication to appear transparent to both the client and the real service, simulating a local interaction across different memory heaps.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
