=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the first three steps of a Remote Method Invocation (RMI). First, the client object calls a method on a local client helper. Second, the client helper packages the call details (method name and arguments) and transmits them across the network. Third, the service helper on the server side receives and unpacks this data to invoke the actual method on the real service object. This process allows the client to interact with remote objects as if they were local.

