the stub object?

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains how a Java RMI client retrieves a stub object (the proxy) using the RMI registry. The client performs a ''lookup'' using the static Naming.lookup() method, providing a URL that includes the server''s IP address and the service''s registered name. The client interacts with the service through its remote interface type, meaning it never needs to know the actual implementation class name. Because the lookup method returns an Object, the result must be cast to the specific remote interface.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. What is the purpose of the RMI registry in the process of a client accessing a remote service?
2. Which static method is used to retrieve a stub, and which class does it belong to?
3. What two pieces of information must be included in the URL string passed to the lookup method?
4. Why must the client cast the result of the lookup method to the remote interface type?','09cbef9f-08ef-4c66-95a5-420b74481d9a'::uuid,NULL,NULL,480,511,'2026-05-08 16:43:33.961818+07');
