=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the technical workflow of Java RMI (Remote Method Invocation) during the client-side lookup process. It outlines three critical steps: first, the client queries the RMI registry using a specific name; second, the registry provides a deserialized stub object to the client; and third, the client invokes methods on this stub. The stub acts as a local proxy, allowing the client to interact with the remote service as if it were residing on the local machine.

