blow away the competition!

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment demonstrates the Proxy Pattern in action through a Gumball Monitor test drive. It illustrates how a client application can monitor multiple remote gumball machines by interacting with local proxy objects. These proxies handle the network communication required to fetch location, inventory, and state data. The key takeaway is that the Proxy Pattern provides location transparency, allowing the client to call methods as if they were local, while only needing to manage potential remote exceptions.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
