=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains the internal mechanics of the Remote Proxy pattern using RMI. When a client calls a method on a proxy, the request is forwarded to a remote skeleton, which invokes the method on the actual object. The result is serialized for transport, then deserialized by the proxy for the client. This process allows the client and service to remain largely unchanged, provided they use remote interfaces, handle potential remote exceptions, and utilize a locator service like the RMI registry.

