looking through possible matches; it also makes things a lot more fun.
Your service revolves around a Person interface that allows you to set and get
information about a person:
Here we can get information
about the person’s name,
gender, interests, and Geek
rating (1-10).
We can also set the same
information through the
respective method calls.
setGeekRating() takes an integer
and adds it to the running
average for this person.
This is the interface; we’ll
get to the implementation
in just a sec...
Now let’s check out the implementation...

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces the application of the Protection Proxy pattern through a matchmaking service example in Objectville. It defines a ''Person'' interface that outlines essential methods for getting and setting user profile data, including a unique ''Geek rating.'' This rating system allows participants to evaluate others'' geekiness, which helps with user engagement. The interface serves as a blueprint for controlling access permissions, such as preventing users from rating themselves or altering other people''s personal information.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
