=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces Invocation Handlers as the core mechanism for Java dynamic proxies. When a method is called on a proxy, it is redirected to the handler''s single invoke() method rather than a corresponding method. The invoke() method receives the proxy instance, the specific Method object, and the arguments. This allows the handler to use reflection to decide whether to forward the call to the RealSubject, enabling dynamic control over method execution and access policies at runtime.

