=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains how to implement the InvocationHandler interface to create a dynamic proxy in Java. Using the OwnerInvocationHandler as an example, it demonstrates how to intercept method calls. The handler uses reflection to check method names, allowing ''getter'' methods and most ''setter'' methods, while specifically blocking ''setGeekRating'' to enforce access control. This illustrates the core logic of the Proxy Pattern: controlling access to a real subject by deciding which calls to forward and which to restrict.

