package headfirst.designpatterns.proxy.virtualproxy;
import java.awt.*;
import javax.swing.*;
class ImageComponent extends JComponent {
private Icon icon;
public ImageComponent(Icon icon) {
this.icon = icon;
}
public void setIcon(Icon icon) {
this.icon = icon;
}
public void paintComponent(Graphics g) {
super.paintComponent(g);
int w = icon.getIconWidth();
int h = icon.getIconHeight();
int x = (800 - w)/2;
int y = (600 - h)/2;
icon.paintIcon(this, g, x, y);
}
}

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment completes the implementation of the Virtual Proxy pattern for an Album Cover Viewer. It details how the ImageProxy class uses a background thread to load images asynchronously from a URL, preventing the user interface from freezing. Once the image is retrieved, it triggers a repaint of the component. The segment also defines the ImageComponent class, which acts as a custom Swing component to hold and center the icon for display.

