This segment introduces the Model-View-Controller (MVC) pattern using a music player analogy. It explains that the Model manages data and logic, the Controller handles user input to update the Model, and the View presents the information. When a user interacts with the interface, the Controller tells the Model to change. The Model then notifies the View of the state change, leading to a display update. This separation ensures that data management, user interaction, and visual presentation are handled by distinct components.

