This segment illustrates how MVC integrates three design patterns: Observer, Strategy, and Composite. The Model uses the Observer pattern to notify views and controllers of state changes without being dependent on them. The View and Controller relationship implements the Strategy pattern, where the Controller manages user actions, allowing for interchangeable behaviors. Lastly, the View uses the Composite pattern to manage its nested GUI components. This separation ensures the View focuses on presentation while the Controller translates input into model actions, creating a decoupled, flexible architecture.

