wrapped heart model.

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment explains how the Adapter Pattern is used within MVC to bridge incompatible interfaces. By creating a HeartAdapter that implements BeatModelInterface, a HeartModel (which uses getHeartRate) can be reused by views and controllers designed for a BeatModel (which uses getBPM). The adapter translates relevant method calls while implementing incompatible actions, like setting heart rate or turning it off, as "no ops." This technique demonstrates how to adapt a new model to work seamlessly with existing architecture without modifying the original code of the view or controller.

