This segment illustrates how the QuackCounter decorator is updated to maintain compatibility with the Observer Pattern. Because the Quackable interface now extends QuackObservable, the QuackCounter must implement observer registration and notification. It does this by delegating these method calls to the underlying Quackable object it is decorating. This ensures that while the decorator adds quack-counting functionality, it does not interfere with the duck''s ability to be observed by other components like a Quackologist.

