public void registerObserver(BeatObserver o) {
beatObservers.add(o);
}
public void notifyBeatObservers() {
for (int i = 0; i < beatObservers.size(); i++) {
BeatObserver observer = (BeatObserver)beatObservers.get(i);
observer.updateBeat();
}
}
public void registerObserver(BPMObserver o) {
bpmObservers.add(o);
}
public void notifyBPMObservers() {
for (int i = 0; i < bpmObservers.size(); i++) {
BPMObserver observer = (BPMObserver)bpmObservers.get(i);
observer.updateBPM();
}
}

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment details the core operational logic of the BeatModel in a DJ application. It implements the Runnable interface''s run method to maintain a beat loop, calculating timing based on Beats Per Minute (BPM). The code also showcases the Observer Pattern in action, providing methods to register and notify two distinct types of observers: BeatObservers and BPMObservers. This ensures that any change in the model state, like a new beat or a modified BPM, is immediately communicated to the registered view components.

