public void notifyBPMObservers() {
for(int i = 0; i < bpmObservers.size(); i++) {
BPMObserver observer = (BPMObserver)bpmObservers.get(i);
observer.updateBPM();
}
}
}

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment details the implementation of the HeartModel class, which simulates a heartbeat. It demonstrates the Observer pattern by managing two distinct sets of observers: BeatObservers and BPMObservers. The code includes logic to calculate heart rate fluctuations, notify observers when a beat occurs or the BPM changes, and provide methods for observer registration and removal. This model serves as the data source in a Model-View-Controller (MVC) structure, illustrating how a concrete model handles state updates and communication.

