564	 	 Chapter 13
what you’ll learn from the guide
The Objectville Guide to
Better Living with Design Patterns
Please accept our handy guide with tips & tricks for living with patterns in the real
world. In this guide you will:
)   Learn the all too common misconceptions about the definition of a
“Design Pattern.”
)   Discover those nifty Design Patterns catalogs and why you just have to
get one.
)   Avoid the embarrassment of using a Design Pattern at the wrong time.
)   Learn how to keep patterns in classifications where they belong.
)   See that discovering patterns isn’t just for the gurus; read our quick
How To and become a patterns writer too.
)   Be there when the true identity of the mysterious Gang of Four is revealed.
)   Keep up with the neighbors—the coffee table books any patterns user
must own.
)   Learn to train your mind like a Zen master.
)   Win friends and influence developers by improving your patterns
vocabulary.

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces a practical guide designed to help developers transition from theoretical knowledge to real-world application of Design Patterns. It outlines several learning objectives, including correcting misconceptions about pattern definitions, utilizing pattern catalogs, and understanding the importance of timing when applying patterns. The guide also covers pattern classification, the identity of the ''Gang of Four,'' tips for writing original patterns, and strategies for improving professional vocabulary to better communicate with other developers in the industry.

