614    Appendix
visitor pattern
Visitor
Use the Visitor Pattern when you want to
add capabilities to a composite of objects
and encapsulation is not important.
Customers who frequent the Objectville Diner and Objectville
Pancake House have recently become more health conscious. They
are asking for nutritional information before ordering their meals.
Because both establishments are so willing to create special orders,
some customers are even asking for nutritional information on a
per-ingredient basis.
A scenario
Lou’s proposed solution:
MenuItem
Menu
Ingredient
MenuItem
Ingredient
// new methods
getHealthRating()
getCalories()
getProtein()
getCarbs()
// new methods
getHealthRating()
getCalories()
getProtein()
getCarbs()
Mel’s concerns...
“Boy, it seems like we’re opening Pandora’s box. Who knows what
new method we’re going to have to add next, and every time we
add a new method we have to do it in two places. Plus, what if
we want to enhance the base application with, say, a recipes class?
Then we’ll have to make these changes in three different places...”

=== SUMMARY ===
This segment introduces the Visitor Pattern as a solution for adding new operations to a composite structure of objects. Using a scenario where a diner needs to provide nutritional information (calories, protein, etc.) for its menu, it highlights the pitfalls of adding methods directly to existing classes. This naive approach leads to code duplication and maintenance difficulties whenever new requirements arise. The Visitor Pattern is recommended when flexibility to add capabilities is needed and strict encapsulation is not the primary concern.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. Under what specific conditions should the Visitor Pattern be used according to the text?
2. What specific nutritional data were customers requesting from the Objectville establishments?
3. Why did Mel object to Lou’s proposed solution of adding methods directly to the MenuItem and Ingredient classes?
4. What potential future addition to the application did Mel mention would further complicate the manual addition of new methods?','e994aec7-5404-41dc-ae4e-67824319d965'::uuid,NULL,NULL,652,531,'2026-05-08 16:43:33.979337+07');
