guide the Visitor through
the Composite structure.
MenuItem
Menu
Ingredient
MenuItem
Ingredient

=== SUMMARY ===
The Visitor Pattern enables adding new operations to a Composite structure without modifying the structure''s classes. It operates alongside a Traverser, which navigates the Composite while the Visitor gathers state from objects. Key benefits include centralized operation code and easy addition of new functionalities. However, drawbacks include weakened encapsulation of Composite classes and increased difficulty in changing the Composite structure itself, as the traversal logic is tightly coupled with the visitor''s requirements.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
1. How do the Visitor and Traverser work together to process a Composite structure?
2. What is the main benefit of using the Visitor Pattern when new functionality needs to be added?
3. Why is the encapsulation of Composite classes considered ''broken'' when using this pattern?
4. How does the Visitor Pattern affect the ease of making changes to the underlying Composite structure?','51dcd816-2826-4ed4-81db-5ce8639c0d3b'::uuid,NULL,NULL,653,629,'2026-05-08 16:43:33.979439+07');
