This index segment provides a detailed guide to software design patterns and principles. It highlights the use of multiple patterns (Compound Patterns) through a duck simulator, the implementation of the Factory Pattern in a Pizza Store project, and the extensive role of the Proxy Pattern, including Remote and Protection Proxies. Key Object-Oriented principles like "Program to an interface, not an implementation," the Principle of Least Knowledge, and polymorphism are also cataloged, providing a structured map for learning robust software architecture and decoupling techniques.

=== REVIEW QUESTIONS ===
